WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.973 --> 00:00:17.316
The next morning at school, everyone was talking about the tornado.

2
00:00:17.336 --> 00:00:19.957
"It went right over Willow Creek!"

3
00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:21.478
exclaimed Carlos.

4
00:00:21.498 --> 00:00:22.898
"It was great!"

5
00:00:22.918 --> 00:00:27.239
"Oh, Carlos," said Katie, rolling her eyes.

6
00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:30.020
"People aren't supposed to like tornadoes."

7
00:00:31.648 --> 00:00:33.870
"Well, I do," said Carlos.

8
00:00:37.452 --> 00:00:40.875
me about your family tornado safety teams," Mr.

9
00:00:40.895 --> 00:00:41.595
Higgins said.

10
00:00:41.615 --> 00:00:43.977
"Did you all have a plan?"

11
00:00:43.997 --> 00:00:48.860
"Katie was our captain," said Joy, smiling at her sister.

12
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.183
"Everybody worked together," added Katie.

13
00:00:53.203 --> 00:00:55.705
"Mom and I made a first aid kit."

14
00:00:55.725 --> 00:00:59.628
"But luckily, we didn't need it," Joy said.

15
00:01:00.776 --> 00:01:03.459
"And Joy found Jellybean after the storm!"

16
00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:04.780
Katie announced.

17
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.204
"Well, Dad and I did," said Joy shyly.

18
00:01:09.224 --> 00:01:13.808
"My house doesn't have a cellar," said Carlos.

19
00:01:13.828 --> 00:01:17.731
"So we decided that a hallway would be the safest place.

20
00:01:18.192 --> 00:01:19.473
There are no windows there."

21
00:01:19.493 --> 00:01:24.297
"Flying glass can be dangerous during a tornado," said Mr.

22
00:01:24.337 --> 00:01:27.460
Higgins. "What about your family, Luke?"

23
00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:31.966
"He forgot to make a plan," tattled Katie.

24
00:01:33.027 --> 00:01:34.308
Luke made a face at her.

25
00:01:34.328 --> 00:01:40.093
"I was at the coffee shop when we heard the tornado warning," he said.

26
00:01:40.113 --> 00:01:45.397
"Mom gave everyone a free fried pie and took them to the basement."

27
00:01:47.078 --> 00:01:51.561
"My dad actually saw the tornado," said Larry Ferguson.

28
00:01:51.581 --> 00:01:55.044
"We all went down into the storm cellar.

29
00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.361
But just before Dad shut the door, he looked up.

30
00:02:00.622 --> 00:02:03.343
The tornado was coming right across the field!

31
00:02:04.563 --> 00:02:07.525
Our barn went up in the air and crashed down hard.

32
00:02:08.685 --> 00:02:10.566
It broke into a hundred pieces."

33
00:02:12.187 --> 00:02:13.667
"Were there any cows in the barn?"

34
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:14.948
asked Carlos.

35
00:02:16.388 --> 00:02:19.750
"No," said Larry, "just my bicycle.

36
00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.590
We haven't found it yet."

37
00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:26.269
"Larry, I'm sorry to hear your barn was destroyed," said Mr.

38
00:02:26.309 --> 00:02:28.991
Higgins. The class nodded.

39
00:02:29.011 --> 00:02:32.294
"Thank you," said Larry.

40
00:02:32.314 --> 00:02:35.276
"But our neighbors are coming over today.

41
00:02:36.257 --> 00:02:38.358
They're going to help Dad build a new barn."

42
00:02:38.378 --> 00:02:41.241
"That's great," said Mr.

43
00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:44.363
Higgins. "It's a big help when people work together."

44
00:02:45.624 --> 00:02:46.165
Then Mr.

45
00:02:46.205 --> 00:02:49.067
Higgins asked Larry what the tornado sounded like.

46
00:02:50.388 --> 00:02:51.849
Larry thought for a moment.

47
00:02:51.869 --> 00:02:56.596
"It sounded like like a "Like a train!"

48
00:02:57.097 --> 00:02:57.777
said Katie.

49
00:02:57.797 --> 00:03:02.859
"Roar!" "It even whistled like a train!"

50
00:03:03.399 --> 00:03:04.120
said Joy.

51
00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:09.542
"Woo-woo!" "I think it sounded like a jet plane," said Carlos.

52
00:03:09.562 --> 00:03:17.525
"Varoom!" "It made a noise," said Laura, "like when we go fast in the car with the windows

53
00:03:17.585 --> 00:03:19.186
down. Whoosh!"

54
00:03:19.206 --> 00:03:23.267
"It was like a wild animal a lion!"

55
00:03:23.688 --> 00:03:24.308
said Luke.

56
00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.343
"Grr!" Everybody started making scary sounds.

57
00:03:36.807 --> 00:03:38.888
COVER!" cried Katie.

58
00:03:40.149 --> 00:03:41.770
That made everybody laugh.

59
00:03:43.591 --> 00:03:44.431
Suddenly Mr.

60
00:03:44.491 --> 00:03:45.872
Higgins waved his arms.

61
00:03:46.452 --> 00:03:47.433
"Quiet, please!"

62
00:03:47.873 --> 00:03:48.433
he called.

63
00:03:48.453 --> 00:03:53.268
"Quiet!" They heard a knock on the door, and Ms.

64
00:03:53.328 --> 00:03:55.210
Olson stepped into the classroom.

65
00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.331
She looked at Mr.

66
00:03:57.351 --> 00:04:02.074
Higgins. "I thought I heard a tornado as I came down the hall," she said.

67
00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:05.016
Everybody laughed again, and Ms.

68
00:04:05.076 --> 00:04:06.077
Olson smiled.

69
00:04:06.097 --> 00:04:09.339
"Mr. Higgins," she said.

70
00:04:09.359 --> 00:04:14.763
"The school yard is covered with tree branches that were blown down during the storm.

71
00:04:15.803 --> 00:04:18.585
Would your class like to help clean up the playground?"

72
00:04:18.605 --> 00:04:22.668
"Yes!" cried all the boys and girls.

73
00:04:23.292 --> 00:04:24.213
"We'll help!"

74
00:04:25.935 --> 00:04:27.857
So when recess came, Mr.

75
00:04:27.897 --> 00:04:30.459
Higgins led the class out to the playground.

76
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.523
They gathered all the branches into a big pile.

77
00:04:35.684 --> 00:04:38.106
Mr. Higgins carried the heavy branches.

78
00:04:38.707 --> 00:04:41.129
Laura helped Joy carry a big branch.

79
00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.473
Carlos found one blue sneaker.

80
00:04:44.953 --> 00:04:47.816
Katie found a broken umbrella under the slide.

81
00:04:49.408 --> 00:04:52.591
Then the kids stood in front of their mountain of tree limbs.

82
00:04:53.071 --> 00:04:54.552
Ms. Olson took a photo.

83
00:04:57.675 --> 00:05:01.838
The next day, she put the photo on the bulletin board in the hall.

84
00:05:03.019 --> 00:05:08.644
Under the photo, she pinned up big letters that spelled "TEAMWORK WORKS!"
